Background work runs under database leases across several worker processes; compose split into `web` and `worker`; docs rewritten to match (spec 25 decisions 7 and 11)
- Improvement-run drivers, the schedule tick and the retention sweep are claimed through lease rows / compare-and-set markers (`src/server/improvementRunLeases.ts`, `improvementRuns.ts`, `schedules.ts`, `retention.ts`), with stale takeover after `workerStaleSeconds` so any number of workers can run side by side and a killed worker's card is resumed.
- `compose.yaml` now defines `web` (`next start`, `RADULF_ROLES=web`, port 3000, `GET /api/health`) and `worker` (`node dist/worker.mjs`, `RADULF_ROLES=worker`, `radulf-worker-health` heartbeat check); only the worker carries the seccomp/AppArmor/systempaths relaxations for the sandbox, both drop all capabilities. `make check-compose` does a throwaway one-web-two-worker run under project `radulf-check`.
- `docs/DOCKER.md` rewritten for the two-service topology (Roles row, `logs -f web worker`, new "Web and worker" section covering shared volume, scaling, reaping and `check-compose`, per-service Day to day, Security posture); `docs/SANDBOXING.md` notes that only the worker container carries the sandbox; `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md` describes the lease model.
